message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Behaviour identifies a low-dimensional parameter subspace tiled by the behavioural repertoire"
authors:
  - family-names: He
    given-names: Chenxi
    affiliation: "Cavendish Laboratory, University of Cambridge"
    email: ch2067@cam.ac.uk
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21594746"
date-released: "2026-07-25"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - behavioural-equivalence manifold
  - identifiability
  - sloppy models
  - neural degeneracy
  - whole-organism simulation
  - Caenorhabditis elegans
abstract: >-
  Code, result files and reproduction container for a study measuring the behavioural-equivalence
  manifold of whole-organism nervous-system simulators across three phyla, showing that behaviour
  constrains a low-dimensional subspace whose extent is set by the richness of the behavioural
  repertoire.
